v.org/abs/2604.06126v1"},{"method":"license_header","retrieved_at":"2026-10-19T06:45:58Z","role":"primary","sha256":"d289e0e1ddfe766ba384068d7cf83848aaf07470f6482711c57ce12763072614","supports":["licenses.code"],"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cmu-l3/gym-anything/HEAD/LICENSE"}],"id":"github:cmu-l3/gym-anything","identifiers":{},"kind":"benchmark","last_verified_at":"2026-10-19T06:44:15Z","licenses":{"code":{"basis":"repository LICENSE header; not a weights/data license","declared":"MIT","retrieved_at":"2026-10-19T06:45:58Z","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cmu-l3/gym-anything/HEAD/LICENSE"},"data":null,"document":null,"weights":null},"links":[{"rel":"primary","url":"https://github.com/cmu-l3/gym-anything"}],"name":"Gym-Anything","notes":"Official code of the Gym-Anything paper. The README describes three parts that can be used separately: the core runtime (src/gym_anything), the CUA-World benchmark (benchmarks/cua_world) and reference agents for Claude, Gemini, Qwen, Kimi and other models. The inspected environment configs (Moodle, Power BI Desktop, an Android AVD calculator and macOS Finder) declare screen observations with mouse and keyboard actions on Ubuntu GNOME, Windows 11, Android AVD 34 and macOS bases; the Finder config also exposes a UI tree, and macOS environments sit in a separate benchmarks/cua_world-macos suite. A task such as moodle_env/enroll_student pairs setup and export hooks with a verifier.py program check and a VLM checklist file. extras/research/software_as_env/creation_audit implements the paper's environment creation-and-audit pipeline, driven by Claude Code by default or Codex CLI. Runners (Docker, Apptainer, QEMU, AVD, AVF, Modal, local and Sandweave) differ in caching, snapshot and recording support. Code was read, not run; paper results were not reproduced.","published_at":null,"relations":[{"evidence_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cmu-l3/gym-anything/4a8d9672d92d8ff2daef232c4bf9c49d3ac4f2ca/README.md","target_id":"arxiv:2604.06126","type":"documented_by"}],"review_status":"curated","scope":"core","summary":"Runtime and CUA-World task suite that turn real applications on Ubuntu, Windows 11, Android and macOS into screen-observing, mouse-and-keyboard agent environments with setup scripts and program verifiers.","task_classes":["R02.07.01.02"],"topics":["evaluation","sandbox","long-horizon"],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://github.com/cmu-l3/gym-anything"}
